/-!
# N5.b (P4 + S3 on the canonical chart): graph-chart presentation of the geometric blowup map over the centre

Lane G10N5, run 0081.  In the setting of `HironakaG10NfTargetChart`:

* `product_graph_coordinate_ideal` — the zero-plane ideal pulled to the base by the graph isomorphism is generated by
  the graph functions (as the private TN lemma of `HironakaFiniteSectionProductGraph`);
* `centre_eq` (P4) — under the base chart isomorphism the centre ideal `b·𝒪_{X,s₀}` is `(g_i)` (from
  `CanonicalTargetGraph.wholeIdeal`);
* `pivot_zero` (P5) — a pivot strict chart point over the centre has zero pivot coordinate
  (`TargetExplicitNormalLaws.whole_ideal` + G10GL's `pivot_coordinate_eq_zero_of_ne_top`);
* **`presentation_at`** — at a pivot strict chart point `y = chartMap j p` over the centre, the native stalk map of
  `π : Bl_B X → X` is a `GraphChartPresentation` with centre `b·𝒪_{X,π y}`.

No named input.
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency false
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

